Notes for AI coding agents. This is a NanoForge game workspace, written in JavaScript (ES
modules, typed with JSDoc): a client app that runs in the browser and a server app that runs in
Bun. NanoForge is a game engine built on an entity component system (ECS).

## Files

- `nanoforge.config.js`: `type: "workspace"`, with `packages: ["apps/*"]`. Each folder it matches
  is an app with its own `nanoforge.config.js`.
- `apps/client/`, `apps/server/`: the two apps. Each has its own `AGENTS.md`: read the one of the
  app you change.
- `.env`: the `NANOFORGE_*` variables that connect the client to the server (address, TCP and UDP
  ports). Change both sides together. Git ignores it.
- `jsconfig.json`: the type-checking options, extended by each app.
- `package.json`<% if (packageManager === "pnpm") { %> and `pnpm-workspace.yaml`<% } %>: the <%= packageManager %> workspace. Install every app with
  `<%= packageManager %> install` here.

## Commands

`nf` comes from the `@nanoforge-dev/cli` dev dependency. Run it from this folder, as
`<%= nf %> <command>`.

- `nf dev`: rebuilds an app when a file in its `src/` changes, and serves the game on
  http://localhost:3000 with the server running. It hides build errors: run `nf build` to see
  them.
- `nf build`: bundles every app with Bun into its `dist/`. It does not check the JSDoc
  types. `-d apps/client` or `-d apps/server` builds one app.
- `nf start`: runs the last build of both apps.

`nf dev` and `nf start` read `.env` from the folder they run in, so run them here.

## Client and server

- They talk over WebSockets. `nf start` gives `NANOFORGE_CLIENT_X` to the client and
  `NANOFORGE_SERVER_X` to the server, as `X` in the `options.env` of `main`. A plain `NANOFORGE_X`
  goes to both. Everything the client gets reaches the browser: never put a secret there.
  https://docs.nanoforge.eu/docs/cli/configuration/environment-variables
- In the generated game, the server moves the entity and sends its position to every client
  (`apps/server/src/systems/move-2d.system.js`), and the client sets the position it receives
  (`apps/client/src/systems/position-sync.system.js`).
- The apps share no code: each defines its own `Position2D`.

